# Unilever Shelf Understanding — GCP & Vertex AI Gemini Benchmark Suite

A modular, scalable computer vision & multimodal LLM benchmark suite built on **Google Cloud Platform (GCP)** and **Vertex AI (`google-genai`)** for evaluating retail shelf understanding across four decoupled capabilities:

1. **Product Detection (`detection`)**: Locates all product facings on a retail shelf (`[ymin, xmin, ymax, xmax]` normalized 0–1000 coordinates, shelf row, horizontal slot index, and visual cues).
2. **Product Classification (`classification`)**: Classifies shelf products (standalone from raw shelf images or conditioned on detected bounding boxes) into structured Unilever attributes (`brand`, `product_name`, `variant`, `category`, `packaging_type`, `confidence`).
3. **Product Matching & Planogram Compliance (`matching`)**: Associates shelf products against a **Product Catalog** (SKU IDs, titles, visual references) and optionally evaluates compliance against a **Planogram** (`planogram_compliant`, slot sequence verification). Works seamlessly both with and without a planogram bucket.
4. **Fine-Tuning (`fine_tuning`)**: Generates Vertex AI Gemini Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) JSONL datasets (`contents` with `fileData` GCS URIs and target structured JSON outputs), uploads datasets to GCS, supports launching/monitoring Vertex AI tuning jobs (`client.tunings.tune(...)`), and benchmarks domain-tuned inference.

---

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph GCP["Google Cloud Storage & BigQuery (Pluggable Sources)"]
        B1["Shelf Images Bucket\n(gs://...-shelf-images)"]
        B2["Product Catalog Bucket\n(gs://...-catalog-images)"]
        B3["Optional Planograms Bucket\n(gs://...-planograms)"]
        ASSOC["Association Table\n(BigQuery / CSV / JSON / Auto-Discovery)"]
        GT["Ground Truth Source\n(BigQuery / CSV / JSON / Custom Schema)"]
    end

    subgraph Tasks["Separated Benchmark Tasks (shelf_benchmark.tasks)"]
        T1["1. ProductDetectionTask"]
        T2["2. ProductClassificationTask"]
        T3["3. ProductMatchingTask"]
        T4["4. GeminiFineTuningTask"]
    end

    subgraph Models["Vertex AI Gemini Models"]
        M1["gemini-3.8-flash"]
        M2["gemini-3.7-flash"]
        M3["gemini-3.5-flash-lite"]
    end

    subgraph Observability["Reporting & OpenTelemetry"]
        OTEL["OpenTelemetry JSONL Logs & Spans\n(start_time, end_time, input/thinking/output tokens)"]
        REP["Detailed Reports\n- row_level_report.csv / .json\n- benchmark_summary.csv / .json\n- benchmark_report.md"]
    end

    B1 & B2 & B3 & ASSOC --> Tasks
    Tasks --> Models
    Models --> Tasks
    GT --> Tasks
    Tasks --> OTEL
    Tasks --> REP
```

---

## Quick Start (Out of the Box)

### 1. Run the Full Benchmark on `gemini-3.8-flash`, `gemini-3.7-flash`, and `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`

```bash
# Run all 4 separated tasks on the sample GCS bucket image across the newest Gemini 3.x Flash models
.venv/bin/shelf-benchmark \
  --config configs/default_config.yaml \
  --tasks classification detection matching fine_tuning \
  --models gemini-3.8-flash gemini-3.7-flash gemini-3.5-flash-lite
```

### 2. Benchmark Any Local Image (Auto-Uploading to GCS) or Specific Model

```bash
.venv/bin/shelf-benchmark \
  --image shelf-image.png \
  --upload-to-gcs \
  --tasks classification \
  --models gemini-3.8-flash gemini-3.7-flash gemini-3.5-flash-lite
```

### 3. Run Without a Planogram Bucket

```bash
.venv/bin/shelf-benchmark \
  --planogram-bucket none \
  --tasks detection classification matching
```

### 4. Run Unit Tests

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest -v
```

